Subject: [PATCH] DV GL: probe GPU processing without GLES extension names

Desktop GL never advertises GL_EXT_float_blend or
GL_OES_texture_float_linear, because both are core there. The DV
capability probe therefore reported no GPU processing, and every Dolby
Vision stream was refused with NoGPUProcessing.

--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLContext.cpp
@@ -1579,8 +1579,8 @@ void CWinSystemGbmGLContext::RefreshDVOutputCapabilities()
     {
       if (auto* renderer = context->Attach())
       {
-        const bool common = pl_opengl_has_ext(context->GL(), "GL_EXT_float_blend") &&
-            pl_opengl_has_ext(context->GL(), "GL_OES_texture_float_linear");
+        // Desktop OpenGL has float blending and linear float filtering in core.
+        const bool common = true;
         caps.processingKnown = true;
         for (unsigned mode = 1; mode < caps.processing.size(); ++mode)
         {
